Add a "Share Aerium" row to the About page, next to Support Aerium.

No share-target API exists on the desktop web platform the way Android's
Intent.ACTION_SEND does - see the Android build's own equivalent feature -
so this copies a one-line pitch plus the download link to the clipboard
instead, for pasting wherever the person wants to send it.

Confirmation is a label swap on the row itself rather than a toast:
chrome://settings mounts no <cr-toast-manager>, unlike chrome://downloads or
chrome://extensions, so calling getToastManager() here would assert instead
of showing anything. The row's own label becoming "Copied to clipboard" for
two seconds needs no extra element and nothing new to mount.

Verified by applying aerium-update-checker.patch and
aerium-about-page-support-link.patch for real against the real files at this
tag, then diffing this change against that result rather than against
pristine - same method aerium-about-page-support-link.patch itself used, and
for the same reason: three of these four hunks land inside text those two
patches already touched.

